{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/367634-the-angel-factory-my-angels-their-infrastructure","id":367634,"title":"The Angel Factory- My Angels & Their Infrastructure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-12T12:01:33-08:00","id":367634,"title":"The Angel Factory- My Angels & Their Infrastructure","content":"So, having recently been given the responsibility of being a GM for a nWoD game set in my hometown of Winnipeg- and being slightly crazy, I went and decided to undertake an absolutely insane endeavour. To create a fully-fleshed angelic hierarchy, with Infrastructure, for the city. These angels are only those that interact with the physical world on a regular basis- they don't include angels working in various 'off-world' conditions.<br /> <br /> A few things to note. I was deeply inspired by Mr. Paraduo's Angelic Hierarchy, and as such my angels have a serial number alongside a name (My personal notes use Enochian glyphs to take the place of letters in the serial number, but the forums probably don't support that). The name is for use amongst other angels, and occasionally cultists, but their human Cover typically has a name as well. Meshing the Cover traits and rules for the Unchained with the increased stats of the Claimed, I think I've given a pretty good model of why angels are such a threat to Demons. Especially since mine use Embeds and possess an Angelic Form as well as wielding Numina and Influences. My first angel is, technically, a bit of a cop-out, since I figured it would be easy enough to take the quickstart and add my own flare to it as a way to introduce my players to the nWoD, but it gives a pretty good idea of how I've decided to design my angels when compared to the original version.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <b><u>Quorum</u></b><b> (</b>John Hu, <b>S</b><b>-1:NA</b><b>/C</b><b>/M</b><b>/W</b><b>:1-P</b><b>-4</b>)<br /> <br /> In charge of Logistical Infrastructure out on the Falcon Lake Lotions farm. Surprisingly, Quorum is quite adept at combat, as his Facility is too far away from the city for a Destroyer or Guardian to arrive in time to help in times of crisis.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>Attributes</i> [If Quorum Falls, then the traits in parentheses take effect]<br /> <b>Physical- </b>Strength: 4 (3) Dexterity: 4 (3) Stamina: 3 (2)<br /> <b>Mental- </b>Intelligence: 3 (2) Wits: 4 (3) Resolve: 3 (2)<br /> <b>Social- </b>Presence: 1 Manipulation: 2 Composure: 4 (3)<br /> <br /> <i>Factors</i><br /> <b>Size- </b>5 (Adult Human) <b>Health-</b> 8 <b>Willpower- </b>7 <b>Defense-</b> 7 <b>Initiative- </b>8 <b>Speed- </b>13<br /> [<b>Cover-</b> 7] <b>Rank-</b> 1 <b>Max Essence- </b>10 [<b>Primum- </b>1 <b>Aether- </b>10/1 <b>Max Covers- </b>1]<br /> <b>Ban- </b>Cannot put down cell phone, or discorporate for 4 hours. Duplicates remain<br /> <b>Bane- </b>Tetrahedrons<br /> <br /> <i>Skills</i><br /> <b>Physical- </b>Athletics: 3 Brawl: 4 Firearms: 3 Stealth (Remaining Unnoticed): 3<br /> Weaponry: 2<br /> <b>Mental- </b>Computer: 4 Crafts: 3 Investigation: 3 Science (Botany): 3<br /> <b>Social- </b>Intimidation: 2 Streetwise (Winnipeg): 2<br /> <br /> <b>Influences-</b> Electricity: 2 <b>Virtue- </b>Precise <b>Vice- </b>Curious<br /> <br /> <i>Numina</i><br /> <b>Implant Mission: </b>Spend 2 Essence, roll Intelligence + Manipulation. Those affected by the Numen are informed of what the entity desires through a vision, and obtain the Obsessed condition to carry it out.<br /> <b>Fork: </b>Spend 5 Essence, roll Intelligence + Composure and touch a large mirror. The duplicate has identical traits to the original, except they can\u2019t use this Numen. The original can make as many duplicates as they have Essence. The duplicates can differentiate themselves slightly from the original.<br /> <br /> <i>Embeds</i> [Ones with asterisks will be retained if Quorum Falls]<br /> <b>Authorized (</b><i>Demon: The Descent </i>Pg. 140<b>)* Diversion (</b><i>Demon: The Descent </i>Pg. 140<b>)</b><br /> <b>Idle Conversation (</b><i>Demon: The Descent </i>Pg. 143<b>) Lost in the Crowd (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 145<b>)</b><br /> <b>In My Pocket (</b><i>Demon: The Descent </i>Pg. 143<b>)* Never Here (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 146<b>)</b><br /> <b>Living Recorder (</b><i>Demon: The Descent </i>Pg. 145<b>)* Without a Trace (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 147<b>)</b><br /> <b>Wave Function Collapse (</b><i>Flowers of Hell</i> Pg. 104<b>)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Angelic Form</i> [Ones with asterisks will be retained if Quorum Falls]<br /> <b><u>Modifications</u></b><b>: Fast Attack (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 197<b>)* Resistors (</b><i>FoH</i> Pg. 124<b>)</b><br /> <b>Unyielding Vise (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 124<b>)*</b> <b>Rivet Arm (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 124<b>)*</b><br /> <b><u>Technology</u></b><b>: Electric Jolt (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 201<b>) Mirrored Skin (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 203<b>)* </b><br /> <b>Savant Core (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 125<b>)*</b><br /> <b><u>Propulsion</u></b><b>: Plasma Drive (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 204<b>)</b>*<b> Spatial Distortion (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 204<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Process</u></b><b>: Wound Healing (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 209<b>)*</b> <b>Nanobot Composition (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 128<b>)</b></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Falcon Lake Lotions</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This particular facility is the culmination of several pieces of simple Concealment Infrastructure supporting an important piece of Logistical Infrastructure which could aid in facilitating smoother operations for the God-Machine and its angels in Winnipeg and the surrounding area. To all intents and purposes, it looks like a simple lavender farm with on-site processing facilities. However, in reality, it is a recycling plant for the God-Machine nearing completion. All it needs now is a few more Demons to act as the refining engines- turning Aether back into Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Concealment:</b> The farm itself serves as concealment- the various buildings, the gift store, and the lavender fields -all of it serves to conceal what\u2019s really going on at the farm. However, there are other pieces of Infrastructure concealing the Facility from prying eyes. The Linchpin of the ferry system is its route. While the ferry is important, it can be replaced. The real linchpin is beneath the water. To get to the farm, one must take a ferry across Falcon Lake, and buried beneath the ferry\u2019s highly specific \u201cscenic\u201d route are submerged containers in the lakebed which are etched with numerous occult symbols, and in fact are filled with various products from the farm. The ferry\u2019s seating plan is arranged to evoke significant mathematical and geometric patterns- which when combined with the cramped conditions of the boat, funnels the Essence of mixed boredom and annoyance into the containers, which combines with the Essence of calm the lavender produces, and ultimately mixes into an aura of blissful ignorance on the farm itself. In the winter, when the farm \u2018closes\u2019 and visitors stop coming, this additional layer of Infrastructure begins to wear thin, but is revitalized by the first ferry trip of the spring. The Logistical Infrastructure of the recycling plant is concealed beneath the lavender field itself. Ports will be hidden beneath particularly large plants, while the Linchpin is a robust example of cryptoflora.<br /> <br /> <b>Logistics:</b> Angels need Essence to keep running, and Aether is useless to the God-Machine. Not only can angels not use it, but Aether runoff can create cryptids that make concealment more difficult. This recycling plant, hidden deep within the south field, funnels the recycled Essence into the Linchpin, which is connected to the processing plant on-site. The Essence is imbued into objects that eventually find their way into the hands of angels, typically via surplus stocks that are supposedly donated to charities. Currently, until the core Infrastructure of the facility is completed, the Aether generated by the occult matrix of the Concealment Infrastructure is simply pumped into the fields as the God-Machine has found that lavender cryptoflora is very useful in creating mind-altering substances that can be absorbed through pores in the skin. These include all products made on-site. They are distributed through commercial channels to stores that carry these products and cater to a local market. These will continue to be produced after the recycling plant is completed. When/if the recycling plant is completed, the Essence filled product will be transported via unmarked vans to U-Haul facilities where they will remain overnight, and will be picked up by a cultist-run dummy corporation the next morning. They are then stored in supposedly defunct warehouses that are owned by a shell corporation of the cult, where individual shipments will be picked up by members of a second cult and dead-dropped at several thrift shops around the city, where they will be retrieved by members of the angels\u2019 staff posing as charity workers.<br /> <br /> <b>Angel Summoning:</b> In order to summon an angel, an occult matrix must be formed, Essence must be gathered, and Infrastructure must be in place. At Falcon Lake Lotions, all of these are fully supported. The ferry ticket stand and loading dock serves as Concealment for it, and houses most of the strange technology necessary to facilitate it, but the true engine of the angel summoning is in the public bathroom attached to the building. A circuit is completed when the ferry docks. The mathematical and geometric designs which reacted with the occult matrix running the Concealment Infrastructure on the farm resonates with similar occult patterning in the building, causing tickets which are purchased there to be treated as sacrifices, every four tickets producing a single measure of Essence. Ultimately, in order for the summoning to be effective for this particular angel, 22 Essence must be generated. However, the angel burns one Essence a day to stay alive while it waits, incorporeal, in this building, and after a couple of days, the Essence burns out and Aether leaks into the lake. This produces the occasional cryptid. The bathroom itself is Logistical in nature. The motion activated hand dryer scans fingerprints and assesses the aura of a potential target, the toilet samples epithelials and runs DNA for compatibility, and the way the target responds to various posters and potential problems with the bathroom- a jammed door, lack of toilet paper, etc. -assesses their rough capabilities. If all the boxes are checked, the bathroom locks and this triggers an occult matrix that violently sacrifices the person, then reconstitutes them as a Cover for the angel. By the time the door has unlocked, everything appears normal and the angel is embedded into its Cover. The person cannot be rescued or recovered- they only exist to conceal the identity of the angel now. The Linchpin of this particular bit of Infrastructure is the smoke detector in the exact centre of the roof, hidden behind a protective metal cage.<br /> <br /> <b>NOTE:</b> If a Demon enters the bathroom, its scanners will figure it out, and the character receives the Flagged Condition. Chances are, any Demons investigating the farm won\u2019t determine the purpose of the bathroom, and will only see it as part of the Concealment Infrastructure. Most will leave it alone. If Quorum Falls or dies, and the facility remains active, a new angel will be crafted, a new Cover will be produced, and work on the site will continue. If he dies and one or more of his duplicates is still alive, one of them retains the Cover, the other shares the Cover, or simply becomes a guardian of the site, maybe being reworked by the God-Machine into a true Guardian or Destroyer. If he Falls, then the remaining duplicates share the Cover, and may or may not always have a bead on where he is at any given moment.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-12-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:19:31-08:00","id":368070,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Boel</u></b><b> (</b>Gregory Markov, <b>S</b><b>-1:/NA</b><b>/C</b><b>/M/W</b><b>:1-G</b><b>/S</b><b>-1)</b><br /> <br /> Boel means \u201cGod is in him\u201d and that is a suitable name for this angel. It is one of a group of prototype angels with the prayers of Benedictions written into their code that can be accessed as Embeds. He serves as one of the more secretive angels in Winnipeg, under a group of Analysts. As per the nature of Analysts and the God-Machine's experiments, Boel and his kin are almost entirely unknown to the rest of the angels in the city.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attributes<br /> <b>Physical-</b> Strength: 5 (4) Dexterity: 4 (2) Stamina: 4 (3)<br /> <b>Mental- </b>Intelligence: 3 (1) Wits: 4 (3) Resolve: 3 (2)<br /> <b>Social- </b>Presence: 3 Manipulation: 3 (2) Composure: 4 (3)<br /> <br /> <i>Factors</i><br /> <b>Size-</b> 5 (Adult Human) <b>Health-</b> 9 <b>Willpower-</b> 7 <b>Defense- </b>8 <b>Initiative- </b>8 <b>Speed- </b>14<br /> <b>Rank-</b> 1 <b>Max Essence- </b>10<br /> <b>Ban-</b> If commanded to identify himself in Russian, Boel will recite his serial number and a significant line of code, which happens to be a protective benediction [<i>H:tV</i> Pg. 159- roll Resolve + Rank, the angel is protected by a barrier that extends five yards in all directions around it, and can only be crossed by a being with Presence greater than the angel\u2019s Presence + Supernatural Trait]<br /> <b>Bane-</b> Any depiction of St. Agrippina of Mineo [It interacts badly with a core segment of code; the Benediction that is recited if it is commanded to identify itself]<br /> <br /> <i>Skills</i><br /> <b>Physical- </b>Athletics: 4 Brawl: 3 Drive: 1 Firearms: 3 Stealth: 3 (Shadowing Targets) Weaponry: 2<br /> <b>Social-</b> Intimidation (Physical Threats): 3 Streetwise (Winnipeg): 2 Subterfuge: 2<br /> <b>Mental- </b>Investigation: 1 Medicine: 1 Occult: 2<br /> <br /> <b>Influences- </b>Fear: 2 <b>Virtue- </b>Suspicious <b>Vice- </b>Dispassionate<br /> <i>Numina</i><br /> <b>Omen Trance:</b> Once every 24 hours, the entity may enter a trance to gain a vision of the future- typically warnings of danger. It spends 1 Essence if it\u2019s on its own behalf, and spends 3 Essence if it\u2019s for someone else. Roll Wits + Occult<br /> <b>Pathfinder: </b>Determines the quickest route to a destination. Spend 1 Essence; the effect lasts for the scene, during which time the entity should be able to get there. If the destination is a Safe Place, the roll is contested by the lowest Resolve + Supernatural Trait among the owners. Roll Intelligence + Streetwise<br /> <br /> <i>Embeds</i><br /> <b>Ambush (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 132<b>) Check Backdrop (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 133<b>) Strike First (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 138<b>) </b><b>Read Hostility (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 137<b>)<br /> Shift Consequences (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 137<b>) Synthesis (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 138<b>) Soup Up (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 99<b>)<br /> Armour of St. Martin (</b><i>H:tV</i> Pg. 158<b>) The Boon of Lazarus (</b><i>H:tV </i>Pg. 160<b>) Wrathful Sword of St. Michael the Archangel (</b><i>H:tV </i>Pg. 163<b>)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Angelic Form</i><br /> <b><u>Modifications</u></b><b>:</b> <b>Blade Hand (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 197<b>) Inhuman Reflexes (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 198<b>) </b><br /> <b>Night Vision (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 198<b>) Steel Frame (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 124<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Technology</u></b><b>: Environmental Resistance (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 202<b>) </b><br /> <b>Glory and Terror (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 203<b>) Mind Reading (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 203<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Propulsion</u></b><b>: Plasma Drive (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 204<b>) Tether (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 204<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Process</u></b><b>: Aegis Protocol (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 205<b>) Quill Burst (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 207<b>)</b></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>Holy Trinity Ukrainian Orthodox Church</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Like virtually every religious institution the God-Machine has hijacked instead of creating, very little of the Infrastructure here has anything, at all, to do with the priest, the church\u2019s finances, or the congregation. In spite of the dogma and cultural outlook of some of these older, more traditional churches, most of the parishioners are not easily susceptible to a cult mindset, and many are simply too darn stubborn to be persuaded by all but the most potent Embeds. It isn\u2019t worth the Essence to use various Numina to establish a cult. Instead, this church serves as an important tether point- farming Essence, ascertaining its resonance, and broadcasting that information to Command Infrastructure in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Concealment:</b> Surprisingly, the primary Infrastructure here that serves to camouflage the God-Machine\u2019s work is not inside the facility itself, but directly across the street from it in full view of the church\u2019s doors. The sign for <i>Blackletter Books &amp; Collectibles </i>contains several layered memetic agents, and the Linchpin is a novelty model skull inside the store. The Aether is stored in an air conditioning unit attached to the apartment above the store. The first layer of defense here is an embedded pull. Those stepping out of the church automatically find themselves compelled to look at the sign. The next layer is a simple mind wipe, to make people forget about anything unusual they may have seen inside the church. [Instantly does so against those with a Wits rating of 2 or under] If that doesn\u2019t work, the next layer is a contested roll to compel the individual to call the number advertising psychic readings next to the sign. [Resolve + Supernatural Trait vs. Manipulation + Subterfuge] If they do call, they gain the Amnesia Condition regarding the unusual thing they have just seen, and only remember getting a reasonably good reading from a telephone psychic [who happens to actually be the angel in charge]. One of the Unchained who calls will receive the Flagged Condition, but will not be affected by Amnesia.<br /> <br /> Another piece of Concealment Infrastructure is the crosses atop each of the towers. While they look more or less normal, at sundown on March 27<sup>th</sup> people who find themselves looking carefully can see the shimmering outlines of angelic glyphs along the length of the cross. This serves to encrypt the data the Logistical Infrastructure is sending. The Linchpin is a large stained glass window in the fifth, central tower. One that cannot normally be reached from inside the church. The Aether is stored in an icon of St. John of Damascus that is hidden in a locked chest in the basement of the church.<br /> <br /> <b>Logistics:</b> The only part of the Infrastructure actually inside the church, the four main corner towers and the large central one form a broadcasting array that collects and reads the resonance of Essence before sending it to Command Infrastructure. For some reason, maintaining the Shadow of the North End the way it is happens to be important to the God-Machine, and it will likely oppose any attempt to help the area that can\u2019t be stemmed by the local Spirits. The Linchpin of the Infrastructure is a set of five bells, one set in each tower. Made of cold iron, plated in meteoric nickel, and leafed in blessed silver, when the bells are rung in unison they harvest Essence from the surrounding area, read its resonance, and transmit it to the Command Infrastructure it\u2019s tethered to. Replacing one of the bells would slow the process down, but all five would have to be replaced or destroyed to actually take down the Infrastructure for good. The Aether container for this particular piece of Infrastructure is a finely crafted statue of the archangel Gabriel. The statue has been known to frequently become covered with an unusual patina that is almost like a metallic mold [in fact an example of cryptoflora]. The church staff believes that it is a natural side effect of the metallic compounds in the statue\u2019s enameled surface. On November 8<sup>th</sup> the statue has been known to glow and exude miraculous rosy oil [Aether runoff].<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> Any and all attempts to tamper with the Linchpins triggers a silent alarm that is rigged into the very mind of Boel- he will come running, at the very least, to investigate. The angel is also present for the end of mass at noon every Sunday, when they ring the bells. Boel himself serves as Defensive Infrastructure that supports the Concealment Infrastructure across the street, as he is the proprietor of the store, runs the phone psychic line, lives in one of the apartments above the store, and has been known to make people asking too many questions disappear. Not too hard to do in this neighborhood- sometimes it even can look normal. Others living in the apartments tend to be very nervous and very cautious. They know that the landlord Gregory Markov keeps the gangs from breaking in, but they\u2019re also frightened of him, and kitchen accidents with knives are far too common for it to be a simple accident.<br /> <br /> <b>Angel Summoning:</b> Gregory Markov was an invention of the God-Machine, a clever, well-crafted patchwork Cover made from the failing memories of elderly Eastern European immigrants. As such, when he arrived and took on the job of landlord\u2019s assistant, the people were rather happy and trusting of him- all save one. The true landlord of the time was a stigmatic cultist, who worked to establish the angel\u2019s way into the world by small sacrifices. In the basement of the building, the water heater runs off boiling blood and Essence. Then, the Linchpin was a particular cuckoo clock, but now it is a combination of the boiler itself and the ghost of Dmitri Burkov- whose beloved cuckoo clock is now his Anchor. It is Burkov\u2019s ghost who causes the knife accidents, small sacrifices of blood that run down the drain and somehow, miraculously, make it to the boiler where they continue to fuel the angel Boel.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T19:04:44-08:00","id":369287,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Uvb</u></b><b> (</b>Andrea Friesen, <b>S</b><b>-1:NA</b><b>/C</b><b>/M</b><b>/W</b><b>:1-G</b>/S-2)<br /> <br /> A particularly interesting God-Machine experiment, the angel known as Uvb possesses a prototype core that enables it to ingest and use four different alchemical Elixrs the same way one of the Ascending Ones would. The God-Machine wants to see if, divorced from an environment where the spiritual belief behind it thrives, can they remain effective?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Attributes<br /> <b>Social- </b>Presence: 4 (3) Manipulation: 1 Composure: 4 (3)<br /> <b>Mental-</b> Intelligence: 2 Wits: 4 (3) Resolve: 3 (2)<br /> <b>Physical- </b>Strength: 3 (2) Dexterity: 5 (2) Stamina: 3 (2)<br /> <br /> <i>Factors</i><br /> <b>Size- </b>5 (Adult Human) <b>Health-</b> 8 <b>Willpower- </b>7 <b>Defense-</b> 6 <b>Initiative- </b>8 <b>Speed- </b>13<br /> <b>Rank- </b>1 <b>Max Essence- </b>10<br /> <b>Ban-</b> Must answer any and all questions of an individual they are assigned to protect, even if the answers are covert or would reveal their supernatural nature.<br /> <b>Bane-</b> Clean agent fire extinguishers<br /> <br /> <i>Skills</i><br /> <b>Mental- </b>Computer: 2 Crafts: 4 (Elixirs) Investigation: 3 Medicine: 2 Occult: 1<br /> <b>Physical-</b> Athletics: 2 (Running) Brawl: 2 Firearms: 1 Larceny: 3 Weaponry: 1<br /> <b>Social- </b>Intimidation: 2 Persuasion: 2 Streetwise (Winnipeg): 3<br /> <br /> <b>Influences-</b> Honesty: 1 Trust: 1 <b>Virtue- </b>Efficient <b>Vice- </b>Open<br /> <i>Numina</i><br /> <b>Blast (\u201cABC\u201d Dry Chemical):</b> For every dot of Strength and Presence, this power gets a range of 10 yards. Rolling Dexterity + Firearms, if successful, this Numen counts as a +0L weapon. You can increase the lethality by spending 2 Essence for each point of lethal damage.<br /> <b>Speed: </b>The entity accelerates into a blur of movement. The entity chooses whether to spend 2 or 4 Essence when activating this Numen. Spending 2 Essence doubles its Speed for the remainder of the scene, while spending 4 Essence triples it.<br /> <br /> <i>Embeds</i><br /> <b>Ambush (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 132<b>) Check Backdrop (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 133<b>) Turn Blade (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 139<b>)</b><br /> <b>Download Knowledge (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 133<b>) Like I Built It (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 135<b>)</b><br /> <b>The Map is not the Territory (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 136<b>) Right Tools, Right Job (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 137<b>)</b><br /> <b>Tools into Toys (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 139<b>) Call Out (</b><i>FoH</i> Pg. 97<b>) Data Retrieval (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 97<b>)</b><br /> <b>Data Wipe (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 98<b>) Open Sesame (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 99<b>)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Angelic Form</i><br /> <b><u>Modifications</u></b><b>: Fast Attack (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 197<b>) Inhuman Reflexes (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 198<b>) </b><br /> <b>Sonic Acuity (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 199<b>)</b> <b>EMP Field (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 197<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Technology</u></b><b>: Acidic Spit (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 199<b>) Essence Drain (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 202<b>)</b><br /> <b>Elixir Core- </b>The angel can use four different Elixirs. Using one takes a reflexive action and a roll of Wits + Rank. <b>[Bennu-Bird Feather (</b><i>H:tV </i>Pg. 174<b>) Mind-Talking Drug (</b><i>H:tV </i>Pg. 175<b>)</b> <b>Mesmeric Vapors (</b><i>H:tV </i>Pg. 177<b>)</b> <b>Liar Pills (</b><i>MR </i>Pg. 130<b>)]</b><br /> <b><u>Propulsion</u></b><b>: Long Limbs (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 204<b>) Plasma Drive (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 204<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Process</u></b><b>: Body Modification (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 205<b>) Extra Mechanical Limbs (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 206<b>)</b></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Soul Gallery Inc<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Not all Infrastructure needs to be an obvious, stand-alone structure, or accomplish extremely unusual effects. Most examples, even full facilities, prefer to instead piggy back off of pre-existing mortal institutions, and use as little supernatural intervention as possible. With Winnipeg, the problem isn\u2019t a lack of support or resources, but a lack of a number of people. Paradoxically, the more people live in a city, the larger it is, the easier it is for the God-Machine to affect causality or edit people, places, or things out of existence. In a city like Winnipeg, you need misdirection, and this bit of Infrastructure helps support that in full.<br /> <br /> <b>Concealment: </b>In the gallery, there is a single bronze piece- a flat disk with arcane symbols engraved beneath the surface -that is tied to an identical piece that was more obviously engraved with positive imagery that sits at the centre of a labyrinth at the nearby Pembina Fisher Park. These two together are the Linchpin. Any efforts to destroy one without destroying the other simultaneous will trigger additional Infrastructure meant to defend the site. Individuals passing the park are compelled to go and walk it, and in spending a few minutes walking serenely, meditating, finding oneself, they lose the destination at the core. The journey becomes more important than the destination, and as such, it becomes more difficult to find the magically connected gallery. It most definitely helps that the gallery is in a private residence that is only available to the public for a very limited time each month. The Aether receptacle is a large block of clay in the basement that always seems to replace itself, and when fired creates pottery that is much more durable than normal. Andrea Friesen has taken credit for this, and claims that it is from a particular deposit up north which gives it these special durable properties. As Andrea is always at the gallery before anyone else, no one questions that she replaces the clay.<br /> <br /> <b>Logistics: </b>The main Infrastructure here is supported directly by the angel known as Uvb. It doesn\u2019t really require Essence, nor does it need an Aether receptacle, because it is supported by the work of the angel\u2019s hands. Any and every statue she makes is intended to evoke a specific response, which will then turn it into the focal point, perhaps even the Linchpin, of a God-Machine plan in the future. The gallery is frequented by members of a different angel\u2019s staff, always on the lookout for suitable pieces to set up the groundwork for altering reality or causality itself.<br /> <br /> More advanced Logistical Infrastructure is hidden behind another wall of Concealment Infrastructure. In the gallery is a guest book with a metal cover that is always warm to the touch. Using a pen that uses a mixture of Aether and blood for ink, a cultist signs their true name, and where they\u2019re taking that particular art piece. After doing so, their name changes to an ironclad false identity with some inane comment about the beauty of art attached to it. Any attempt to trace the buyer\u2019s financials suffers the same supernatural hindrance if they were to attempt to trace the buyer themselves. The Linchpin to the Concealment Infrastructure is the pens. They always use the same model to sign, and to remove the Infrastructure every pen must be destroyed. The Aether receptacle for the Concealment Infrastructure is a vat of blood at an undisclosed location that must always remain at body temperature unless in use. The Linchpin for the Logistic Infrastructure is the guest book itself. From the moment a cultist signs it, it inputs the information about where to ship the art piece into the GPS of several delivery trucks at a warehouse near the airport. The drivers are oblivious to what the trucks are being used for, but find it odd they don\u2019t ship much more than art. Destroying the guest book obliterates the GPS data, and unless more overt action is taken, the art pieces won\u2019t make it to where they need to go. The Aether receptacle is a decorative crystal orb attached to a chandelier in the basement.<br /> It is worth noting that while the angel known as Andrea Friesen is the only supernatural being at the gallery, art is still well known for being able to generate Essence, especially that tied to emotions. Those who come to the gallery are always on the lookout for other pieces that could serve as the focal point for Essence farms or be used to begin to alter the Shadow of an area if used as urban art.<br /> <br /> <b>Defense: </b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">All attempts to tamper with the Linchpins pull at the attention of Uvb. The angel counts as a piece of Infrastructure herself. Depending on the severity of the assault, she may even shed human form and go on the assault. However, that\u2019s the least of a Demon\u2019s worries, as trying to take down the primary Concealment Infrastructure is problematic in and of itself, and destroying any other Linchpin is less overt but equally as likely to get one of the Unchained in trouble with the proprietor, and maybe the police. If a ring of Demons does the impossible and takes down the Concealment Infrastructure, a defensive failsafe kicks in. Hidden behind a decorative shield on the wall is an antique clock, this clock is always tied to the Linchpin, which is an identical clock in Andrea Friesen\u2019s studio apartment in Osborne Village. In the event that one of the Linchpins for the Concealment Infrastructure is deactivated, the failsafe reverts time back to whatever time it says on the clock. Anyone involved is transported back to wherever they were at that time. The Aether receptacle is a paper shredder in the apartment.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Angel Summoning: </b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Andrea Friesen was originally a person, a starving artist trying to live her dream in Osborne Village. She eventually stumbled upon one of the God-Machine\u2019s reality alteration rooms, which she used profusely in an effort to improve her life, and give her more time to focus on art. As she grew less and less focused on life, she became more and more obsessed with perfecting her art; leading to very valuable sculptures she created being destroyed by her hand- in reality, sacrifices to the angel waiting in the wings. When she was eventually erased, the angel was ready to step into her shoes, and did so. It continues to make, and then sacrifice, beautiful statues to keep itself running, and the small studio apartment is connected to a Bolthole via a closet. The Bolthole is equipped with a full chemistry lab, which is never empty, so that it can replenish its Elixirs, and a full armory. It is also attached via another door to a broom closet at the gallery, enabling Uvb to get to the site extraordinarily quickly. The Aether receptacle for her summoning and continued survival is a toolbox for her art in the apartment. Most of the art implements are now embedded gadgets.</span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-15-2015, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T16:56:41-08:00","id":375688,"title":"","content":"<b><u>X-C:H/39</u></b><b>: (</b>Josiah Miller, <b>S</b><b>-1:NA</b><b>/C</b><b>/M</b><b>/W</b><b>:1-G</b><b>/S-4)</b><br /> <br /> An experiment by the God-Machine into whether angels operating as Claimed would make effective agents. Fused with a human psyche, they would be closer to the Unchained condition, and bonded to their host they\u2019d be unable to Fall. So far, no one has been able to take the full load for very long- the angel\u2019s AI-like psyche is anathema to the human brain, and eventually they destroy each other. This particular example manifests a few form powers, but otherwise uses fairly mundane magic alongside Embeds.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>Attributes</i><br /> <b>Social-</b> Presence: 3 (2) Manipulation: 6 (3) Composure: 3<br /> <b>Mental-</b> Intelligence: 2 Wits: 4 (3) Resolve: 3 (2)<br /> <b>Physical-</b> Strength: 2 (1) Dexterity: 3 Stamina: 3 (2)<br /> <br /> <i>Factors</i><br /> <b>Size- </b>5 (Adult Human) <b>Health- </b>8 <b>Willpower-</b> 6 <b>Initiative- </b>6 <b>Defense- </b>5 <b>Speed- </b>10<br /> <b>Rank- </b>1 <b>Max Essence- </b>10<br /> <b>Ban- </b>If a person threatens harm to themselves or others that cannot serve to produce Essence for the God-Machine, the angel must try and talk them down.<br /> <b>Bane- </b>An incident report from before Josiah Miller was Claimed by the angel, detailing one occasion where he was unable to prevent someone killing themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Skills</i><br /> <b>Social-</b> Empathy: 2 Intimidation (Interrogations/Physical Threats): 3<br /> Persuasion (Negotiation/Seduction): 3 Streetwise (Winnipeg): 2 Subterfuge: 1<br /> <b>Physical-</b> Athletics (Pursuit): 2 Brawl: 2 Firearms (Precision/Cover): 3 Larceny: 2<br /> <b>Mental-</b> Computer: 1 Investigation: 2 (Crime Scenes/Records) Politics (Police Force): 1<br /> <br /> <b>Influences-</b> Gravity: 1 Calm: 1 <b>Virtue- </b>Amiable <b>Vice- </b>Procedural<br /> <br /> <i>Merits</i><br /> <b>Professional Training (</b>Police<b>): </b>5 \u00bb Contacts (Police Chief\u2019s Office, Missing Persons\u2019)<br /> <b>Fleet of Foot: </b>2 <b>Status (</b>WPD<b>):</b> 4 <b>Unseen Sense (</b>God-Machine<b>):</b> 2 <b>Aura Reading:</b> 3<br /> <b>Biokinesis: </b>2 <b>Psychokinesis (</b>Electricity<b>):</b> 5 <b>Psychometry:</b> 3<br /> <br /> <i>Embeds</i><br /> <b>Ambush (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 132<b>) Check Backdrop (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 133<b>) Synthesis (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 138<b>)</b><br /> <b>Shift Consequences (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 137<b>) Cool Heads Prevail (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 126<b>) </b><br /> <b>Devil\u2019s Advocate (</b><i>D:tD</i> Pg. 126<b>)</b> <b>No Quarter (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 130<b>) </b><br /> <b>Shifty Eyes (</b><i>D:tD</i> Pg. 132<b>) Special Someone (</b><i>D:tD</i> Pg. 132<b>) </b><br /> <b>Find the Leak (</b><i>D:tD</i> Pg. 150<b>)</b></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 151 Princess Street<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Not strictly speaking a true God-Machine facility, there is still some limited Infrastructure embedded within the Winnipeg Police Service. The core of that Infrastructure is Logistical, but some minor degree is Defensive. However, this is almost entirely unintentional, as the only reason this Infrastructure has been set up is thanks to the desperate efforts of an experimental angel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Logistical:</b> Crafted together mostly with great effort, lots of tinkering, and a good deal of pull around the office, four key data storage servers- normally encrypted to protect the sensitive case information contained within -have been tethered together by the cunning angel to help inform the God-Machine\u2019s operations. It\u2019s more than just incident reports and case files; it\u2019s suspicions, confidential informants, suspected cults, leads, rumors, stolen identities, and unsolved crimes. With it, the God-Machine can create or erase information in the databases- that includes angelic Covers and the actions of Infrastructure. Each computer is an identical, sleek, modern desktop- but if anyone were to open up the CPU they\u2019d find that it\u2019s beyond anything normal. The Linchpin is the servers themselves. A virus administered directly to their hardware would cripple the police, but it would also disable the Infrastructure. The Aether is contained in a filter inserted into the pipes supplying water to the gun-cleaning station of the armory. As a result, most end up as embedded Gadgets without anyone noticing, which has led to a dramatic increase to the success rate of hits, and a dramatic reduction in officers potentially getting injured.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Defence:</b> The angel itself is the Defence Infrastructure- when something has been flagged by the God-Machine or its analysts, Sergeant Josiah Miller tends to get an email written entirely in machine code, and the four tethered computers all experience a glitch at the same time. This also occurs any time an angel or the God-Machine itself alters some of the information contained within. Regardless of the source, the angel gets the information, and then goes investigating. And if there\u2019s one thing that can shut down supernatural action faster than almost anything else, it\u2019s government intervention.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Angel Summoning:</b> This particular angel wasn\u2019t meant to come into this world. The God-Machine, cruel master that it is, simply created a small, low rank angel, dropped it into an environment where it would begin to bleed Essence, and waited to see what happened. Perhaps unsurprisingly, the angel did exactly as its creator expected- it Claimed a human. The latest in a long line of attempts to have an angel Claim a human, which usually end in disaster, this particular example has done quite well for itself, and so the God-Machine decided to make use of it. This particular angel, seeing as it has no Infrastructure tied to supporting it, relies almost exclusively on Essence farms and sacrificing small things. Everyone knows that, for whatever reason, cell phones never last very long in Josiah Miller\u2019s possession.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-20-2015, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T12:53:53-08:00","id":379428,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, is there a particular reason why you chose to abandon the Angels as Spirits thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T14:37:51-08:00","id":379518,"title":"","content":"Interesting question. It may seem as though I have, but this is really just a preference for having each and every angel be a threat. The fairly low stats of a Rank 1 angel didn't give me that vibe, and I figured that if a Demon used to be an angel, and they have a Cover, the most likely angels to fall and have Covers are the foot soldiers, IE. Rank 1s. I just figured it would be a bit different to have the direct counterparts of the Unchained be such a massive difference in power. They're got a range of form powers similar to a Demon at Primum 10, they have Numina, they have Influences- in other words, they're exactly like Demons, but with a significant power boost. Take Uvb, for example. When you stack up her form powers, like Long Legs and Plasma Drive, then combine them with the Speed Numen, she gets a Speed of roughly 108 for the rest of the scene. Functionally, my players insisted I start treating her unarmed attacks when she's moving that fast like a car crash- and they absolutely loved it. Of course, with one solid hit she can pretty much lay out just about any character not in Demonic Form, but they loved the tension and the skill that fighting something with that sort of overwhelming power came with.<br /> <br /> With angels at Rank 2 and above, they gave the right vibe of threatening power, so they stay with the Ephemeral Beings rules. I still have some Ephemeral Rank 1 angels, and they generally serve as minions for more powerful and influential Rank 2 angels. Speaking of which, here's one slightly more average angels. Bear in mind that these guys are still &quot;experimental&quot; in that they're much more powerful than typical angels. I really messed around with this guy's Angelic Form to make something pretty terrifying, but I might change it later if it doesn't test-play well.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Castiel</u> (S-1:/NA/C/M/W:2-G/S)</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>Attributes</i><br /> <b>Power- </b>5 <b>Finesse- </b>5<b> Resistance- </b>4<br /> <br /> <i>Factors</i><br /> <b>Size- </b>9<b> Corpus- </b>13<b> Willpower- </b>9 <b>Initiative- </b>9 <b>Defense- </b>5 <b>Speed- </b>15 <b>Rank- </b>2<br /> <b>Max Essence- </b>15 <b>Manifestations- </b>Twilight Form, Materialize, Discorporate, Fetter<br /> <b>Ban- </b>The angel must cease what it\u2019s doing (even if it\u2019s in combat), discorporate, and investigate if it is told the location of its Infrastructure and given a credible threat.<br /> <b>Bane- </b>A Masonic ceremonial sword that belonged to Charles Napier Bell [When the Infrastructure was first getting started the angel was a high-rank member of the Freemasons, an abandoned Masonic lodge is where the Infrastructure is stationed]<br /> <br /> <b>Influences-</b> Disgust: 3 Curiosity: 2 <b>Virtue- </b>Concealed <b>Vice- </b>Manipulative<br /> <i>Numina</i><br /> <b>Mortal Mask: </b>This Numen disguises a Materialized entity as a human. Using the Numen costs 1 Essence and the human seeming lasts for activation successes in hours. The human \u201ccostume\u201d is flawed- witnesses may make a Wits + Composure roll penalized by the entity\u2019s Finesse to realize that something is wrong. Characters able to sense the entity in Twilight do not suffer a penalty to the roll.<br /> <b>Fork: </b>Spend 5 Essence, roll Power + Resistance and touch a large mirror. The duplicate has identical traits to the original, except they can\u2019t use this Numen. The original can make as many duplicates as they have Essence. The duplicates can differentiate themselves slightly from the original.<br /> <br /> <i>Embeds</i><br /> <b>Hesitation (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 127<b>) Just Bruised (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 129<b>) Play Possum (</b><i>FoH</i> Pg. 96<b>) </b><b>Special Someone (</b><i>D:tD</i> Pg. 132<b>) Ripple (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 96<b>) </b> <b>Wasted Time (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 100<b>)</b><br /> <b>Ambush (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 132<b>) Check Backdrop (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 133<b>) Momentum (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 136<b>) </b><b>Shift Consequences (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 137<b>) Strike First (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 138<b>) </b><b>In My Pocket (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 143<b>)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Angelic Form</i><br /> <b><u>Process</u></b><b>: Aegis Protocol (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 205<b>) Extra Mechanical Limbs (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 206<b>)</b><br /> <b>Wound Healing (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 209<b>) Nanobot Composition (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 128<b>)</b><br /> <b>Insect Swarm (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 206<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Propulsion</u></b><b>:</b> <b>Phasing (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 204<b>) Teleportation (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 204<b>) </b><br /> <b>Wings (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 205<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Technology</u></b><b>: Essence Drain (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 202<b>) Frost Aura (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 202<b>)</b><br /> <b>Blind Sense (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 200<b>)</b> <b>Shielded Compartment (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 126<b>)</b><br /> <b><u>Modification</u></b><b>: Blade Hand (</b><i>D:tD </i>Pg. 197<b>) Huge Size (</b><i>D:tD</i> Pg. 197<b>) </b><br /> <b>Nauseating Musk (</b><i>FoH </i>Pg. 123<b>)</b></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>335 Donald Street</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">An old facility, the abandoned, boarded up, but still pristine Masonic temple on Donald Street has managed to avoid being torn down, repurposed, or even being sold, for almost fifty years. Completed in 1895, and closed down as a Masonic Temple in 1968, the angel running the Infrastructure, and its minions, managed to have it repurposed as a restaurant in 1978 which served as Concealment while they upgraded the Infrastructure. The building was finally abandoned in 1999, though enterprising businessmen have poured over 3.2 million into upkeep and renovation before mysteriously abandoning their projects. The building is known, in Winnipeg\u2019s occult scene, for being haunted- though not quite in the way they imagine. Sergeant Josiah Miller usually tours the building, for kicks, about once a month.<br /> <br /> <b>Logistics:</b> No one is sure what the original purpose of this Infrastructure was, save for perhaps Castiel, the local Principalities, and the God-Machine, but whatever it was, it took around 73 years for the project to complete. The ritualized and staged process of Masonic rituals, money donated to the temple by a specific internal faction, and art objects that would occasionally go missing fueled the building to do\u2026 something. Whatever it was, it required a ludicrous amount of Essence to pull off, and the neighbourhood has remained incredibly resistant to change ever since, which is probably what this Infrastructure is meant to do now- maintain the status quo. Whatever output this Logistical Infrastructure was supposed to pull off has been completed, and it blankets the area totally. It doesn\u2019t regularly cycle Essence anymore- in fact, it seems like a dead zone, sucking up Essence that goes off to some unknown destination. The Aether, which is by now about 16 years old, still sits in the old oil drums for the fry cookers. No one is really sure if it\u2019s still there, or if Aether that\u2019s been sitting for that long is even safe to use anymore. It could be toxic- even for a Demon.<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> The most obvious form of Infrastructure to this end in the facility is the angel Castiel and its minions- invisible and unseen -that serve as the inspiration for stories of hauntings. The building itself is defended by, apparently, ironclad documents of ownership. The individual who oversaw the sale of the building was working, knowingly or unknowingly, for the God-Machine. Only the rightful owner of the building may do it permanent harm. Otherwise, thanks to the sturdy Logistical Infrastructure, any damage done to the building will simply warp out of reality thanks to the \u201cbackup\u201d that Infrastructure has stored. The Linchpin for this is the bill of sale, and proof of ownership. If a ring of Unchained can obliterate any mention of the current owner\u2019s claim on the property, the Infrastructure will fail. The Aether receptacle is the safety deposit box that the official document is kept in. As a result, it has become something of a metaphysical open space, like a Bolthole, and many \u201cconfiscated\u201d objects- like Gadgets -have ended up in there. Just waiting for an angel, or clever Demon, to pull them out. Beyond just the simple Defense of the building, the building itself appears to form a Linchpin for a larger piece of Infrastructure, which is quite possibly another, larger, layer of Defensive Infrastructure meant to defend something much more important than a simple Facility.<br /> <br /> <b>Angel Summoning:</b> Of course, the most obvious angel is Castiel, but his summoning Infrastructure was in a different place and is long gone. He no longer has any direct support, and instead lures the occasional homeless person down to the basement, where he will sacrifice them to fuel himself. However, something just isn\u2019t right with that picture. Where do his minion angels get their Essence? Why are they always in perfect health with full tanks of Essence? And why, then, does the entire building still vibrate with energy sympathetic to angel summoning? There is no obvious Linchpin, nor is there an Aether receptacle- so where the hell is it all?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T13:39:43-08:00","id":380410,"title":"","content":"I find the mentality that Rank 1 angels are 'foot soldiers' curious given that isn't terribly evident. Rank 1 ghosts are echoes, described as rarely even being intelligent or aware. Rank 1 angels and spirits would be likewise weak? This, to me, implies that angels used as 'foot soldiers' would be Rank 2 and above while Rank 1 angels would be simple processes and support entities.<br /> <br /> I find the most curious thing about your angels is that you gave them an &quot;Angelic Form&quot;. Do you use this in the same way a demon has &quot;Demonic Form&quot;? My angels are simply built with their 'Angelic Form' pre-baked. That's what they are, a big mess of horror, and their 'Cover' is simply the Mortal Mask numen. The revelation of their 'Angelic Form' is simply them turning off Mortal Mask in that case. Was there any particular reason you chose this route or is the 'Angelic Form' here more for book-keeping purposes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T13:54:22-08:00","id":380413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/367634-the-angel-factory-my-angels-their-infrastructure?p=380410#post380410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the mentality that Rank 1 angels are 'foot soldiers' curious given that isn't terribly evident. Rank 1 ghosts are echoes, described as rarely even being intelligent or aware. Rank 1 angels and spirits would be likewise weak? This, to me, implies that angels used as 'foot soldiers' would be Rank 2 and above while Rank 1 angels would be simple processes and support entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the rank 1 angels mentioned in the GMC are messengers and faceless foot soldier assistants. Rank 2 is more fitting for foot soldiers and thugs and unique but hopelessly specialized angels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T13:56:48-08:00","id":380415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/367634-the-angel-factory-my-angels-their-infrastructure?p=380410#post380410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the mentality that Rank 1 angels are 'foot soldiers' curious given that isn't terribly evident. Rank 1 ghosts are echoes, described as rarely even being intelligent or aware. Rank 1 angels and spirits would be likewise weak? This, to me, implies that angels used as 'foot soldiers' would be Rank 2 and above while Rank 1 angels would be simple processes and support entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, considering that our primary examples of Rank 1 angels are Mister Shivers and the Polis Men and the Hunted Condition's definition of a &quot;lesser angel&quot; is Rank 2-3 I'm inclined to agree with the general sentiment here; the implication by Werewolf 1e's Forsaken-totems-as-nearer-to-partners construction, the GMC Rank rules, and spoilers for Mage 2e's changes to familiars is that Rank 2 ephemeral beings tend to be nearest in relatability to an average starting supernatural PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T19:50:09-08:00","id":380702,"title":"","content":"With the Angelic Form, it is mostly just for book-keeping purposes- I needed some way to keep track of all the potential powers the angel has, and to keep a view of its appearance fairly static. I find that if I don't write that stuff down it tends to blur and change. But yes, either they turn it all the way on, or not at all. I do agree that, with the Rank rules as written, a Rank 2 entity is more or less directly comparable with your average starting supernatural PC, but for some unusual reason I can't entirely remember, I decided to differentiate between Rank 1 angels who are purely Ephemeral beings, and those who have a &quot;Cover&quot;, as it were. I think it was partially inspired by a mixture of how Quorum was statted in the quickstart, wondering what happens to &quot;deleted&quot; people from the reality-editing room in the GMC, and this idea just came out of it.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Rank 1 angels still make an appearance, but more so as servants of a more powerful angel. I ended up discussing this with my players while I was building the setting, and they decided that with the size of the city this Chronicle is set in, fighting a Rank 1 Ephemeral angel would feel more like a &quot;Monster of the Week&quot; story than &quot;Holy Crap, enemy agents are everywhere!&quot; I think the decision also had something to do with how the different ranks of angels were described in Mr. Paraduo's Angelic Hierarchy, which has deeply inspired a lot of how I treat angels in my Demon and GMC games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}